# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SHRI-AI — one root .gitignore for the whole repository.
#
# What is committed:
#   client/src/         the website's source (React + Vite)
#   client/public/      static files served as-is, incl. the built photos
#   client/dist/        the built site — tracked on purpose, see "Build output"
#   client/image-src/   photo manifests (sources.json), not the photos
#   client/scripts/     build tooling (npm run images)
#   client/deploy/      server config examples
#
# Patterns without a leading slash match at any depth.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── Unused files ──
# Everything the website does not use: original/source images, design
# exports, retired components and documents. Kept on disk for reference,
# never pushed.
/UN_USED_FILES/


# ── Dependencies ──
# Rebuilt from package-lock.json by `npm ci`; the lockfile stays committed.
node_modules/


# ── Build output ──
# client/dist/ is deliberately committed: the site is deployed by copying the
# built output straight to the web server, with no build step there. Only
# tool caches are ignored.
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.local


# ── Image originals ──
# Full-size photos downloaded by `npm run images` (client/scripts/
# build-images.mjs). Each set's sources.json is the committed record of
# where they come from; the originals are only a local cache, and the
# optimised WebP output in client/public/ is what ships.
client/image-src/**/originals/


# ── Environment files ──
# May hold credentials. Commit a *.env.example template instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example


# ── Logs, caches and coverage ──
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.eslintcache
.cache/
coverage/
.nyc_output/


# ── Editors and tools ──
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
# Merge and backup leftovers
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
# Claude Code local settings and installed skills (`npx skills add`)
.claude/
skills-lock.json


# ── OS files ──
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
# Image-viewer metadata sidecars (these once slipped into client/public/)
.comments/
